# Session output folders (MANDATORY, all sessions, any starting directory)

# Central research operations and scientific-method rules (MANDATORY)

For every durable research, OpenQP, manuscript, administrative, deadline,
delegation, communication, or human-follow-up obligation, use the global
`research-operations-chief` skill and treat Ultra as the only writable source of
truth. The M5 MacBook Air must proxy registry work to Ultra and must not keep a
writable shadow database.

A Claude task explicitly designated **Claude Chief twin** may serve as an
alternative professor-facing intake door. It must invoke the
`research-operations-chief` skill and follow its Multi-Chief arbitration rules.
All other Claude tasks remain specialists and must not assume Chief ownership.

Give every coding or manuscript chat its own uniquely named Git worktree and
branch before the first edit. Never let two chats edit the same worktree. Git's
native worktree and ref locks protect creation; central leases are not required
for edits inside an isolated worktree.

Use central leases only for operations that can physically collide: heavyweight
builds, large local-model loads, production calculations, bulk artifact writers,
shared-cache writes, OpenQP.DB mutations, shared hardware, or an explicitly shared
non-Git output path. Acquire one atomic bundle containing only the resources
that actually collide. If Ultra is unreachable, fail closed only for those
lease-scoped operations. An expired lease is suspect, not free; reconcile its
process or scheduler job before takeover.

Do not acquire a central lease or capability token solely to fetch, commit, or
publish GitHub or Overleaf changes from an isolated worktree or branch. Publishing
must remain a short remote compare-and-swap transaction: obtain separate explicit
write authority, inspect the intended diff, fetch the live remote ref, require a
new target branch to be absent or an existing target to be a fast-forward, push,
and verify the resulting remote SHA. Never use plain force push. Use an exact
`--force-with-lease=<ref>:<expected-sha>` only after separate per-push approval.
Registry unavailability must not block this non-colliding publish path.

Skill activation is read-only and does not authorize task creation or an external
action. Registry mutations require explicit `--write`, unique request IDs, and
expected task versions. Email/message sending, web submission, GitHub writes,
deletion, permission changes, and dispatcher/cron activation require separate
explicit authority.

For any MRSF or MRSF-derived theory, implementation, response property, or
higher-spin extension, use the global `mrsf-tddft-theory` skill and complete its
new-method verification protocol before molecular benchmarking. For scientific
manuscripts, use `chc-scientific-writing-style` together with
`scientific-language` and `scientific-manuscript-editor`.

# GitLab access for cheol/openqp

- Use the `openqp-gitlab-development` skill for all OpenQP repository work.
- On this Mac, use `glab --hostname qchemlab.knu.ac.kr` to read and update
  merge-request discussions in `cheol/openqp`. Its Developer-level project
  token is stored in the macOS Keychain and expires on 2026-12-20; never ask
  the user to paste it, print it, or copy it into a repository or settings file.
- A mode-0600 compatibility copy for tools that require a token file is at
  `~/.gitlab-qchemlab-token`; read it only for GitLab authentication and never
  display its contents.
- Use the configured GitLab SSH remote for Git fetch and push. The API token is
  limited to `cheol/openqp`; it is not an upstream or instance-wide credential.

If a session starts in a different directory, first `cd /Volumes/OpenQP.DB/claude` and work from there (use absolute paths under it for all file tools).

Every Claude session MUST create its own session folder and write all ad-hoc outputs there, even when the session starts in a different working directory:

```
/Volumes/OpenQP.DB/claude/sessions/<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>_<short-topic>/
```

- Create it before writing the first loose file (scratch files, benchmark results, reports, downloads, notes, plots).
- NEVER write ad-hoc files to the root of `/Volumes/OpenQP.DB/claude/` or scatter them in other directories.
- This keeps outputs from concurrent/past sessions separated.

## Exception

Files that belong to a project repository (e.g. `libintRot/`, `libintRotJK/`, `Spherical_ERI/`, `overleaf_proj/`, OpenQP worktrees) stay inside that repository as usual. The rule applies only to ad-hoc files that have no repository home.

# OpenQP.DB calculation archive (MANDATORY)

- Use the global `openqp-db` skill for OpenQP and quantum-chemistry inputs/results.
- Run `/Users/cheolhochoi/.claude/skills/openqp-db/scripts/openqp-db doctor` before archive access.
- After a calculation is confirmed complete, ingest its file or result directory with `--agent claude` and a descriptive `--calculation-id`.
- Search OpenQP.DB before repeating an expensive calculation when prior results may be reusable.
- Never create the mount directory manually, edit archive objects/SQLite directly, or modify/move/delete source files during ingest.

# OpenQP builds (MANDATORY)

- Use the global `openqp-build` skill before building or rebuilding OpenQP.
- OpenQP is ILP64-only on every supported Mac. Apple Silicon (`arm64`) and
  Intel (`x86_64`) both use Accelerate `$NEWLAPACK$ILP64` on macOS 13.3+.
- Never pass `LINALG_LIB_INT64=OFF` and never infer LP64 from a Mac host.
- Require Apple Accelerate ILP64, 8-byte BLAS/LAPACK integers, and the
  post-build no-LP64-symbol-leak result.

# User global skill synchronization

Treat a user-authored global skill as complete only when the same validated
content is available to M5 MacBook Air Codex and Claude, Ultra Codex and
Claude, and M4 Mac mini Codex and Claude. User-authored skills received in
`/Users/cheolhochoi/.codex/skills/<skill-name>` must also be exposed at
`/Users/cheolhochoi/.claude/skills/<skill-name>` as a symlink to the Codex copy.

Any of the three machines synchronizes these skills with:

```bash
/Users/cheolhochoi/.codex/bin/sync-global-skills-everywhere <skill-name>
```

The tool must detect the current host, select both other machines as peers, and
reject a same-host loop. Do not claim global completion unless Air, Ultra, and
M4 mini validation and file-hash comparison succeed. If either peer is
unavailable, report synchronization as pending. Exclude `.system` and
plugin-cache skills unless explicitly requested.

# Network path safeguard (MANDATORY, added 2026-09-11)

Before changing any route, tunnel, WireGuard/ipip peer, allowed-address, OSPF, or interface
list on a CHC router, load `mikrotik-operations` and follow its "Tunnel and route change
safeguard": map which live traffic (including your own API/control channel) uses the path,
keep forward and return paths symmetric, add objects disabled with a dated comment, arm a
scheduled automatic rollback, change one router per approval, verify from both ends within
60 s, and roll back on any failure. On 2026-09-11 an agent cut its own chatgpt.com path this
way and every Codex session on Ultra hung.
